  "name": "Example: Identifying the Net of a Polyhedron",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/f233556f9055563f3956eea7eaf9744fb20993084f4c3eeb5e2e35d730d8d2aa.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the nets above is the net of a rectangular prism?",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/5fc1630e4e44bf68f833004ab975e406b8734fe062849484165310e093d14155.png)\n\n \n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a rectangular prism, as shown below: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/c2f6985ca8cd95a71409936ede80c6f257e863bd459fe5a27178a04ea3edb88c.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that the other two nets have triangular faces, so they cannot be the nets of a rectangular prism. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I.",
